The passages do not say what model RC-5 is, so they give no basis for naming a specific procedure for it. Nothing in them describes RC-5's characteristics, its intended use, or whether it is a safety component or has self-evolving behaviour. They also give no 20 January 2027 date or rule tied to that date.

The passages state only general principles. Recital 54 of the Regulation says a safety component, or a system with self-evolving behaviour ensuring safety functions, should be assessed by a third party. Recital 20 says certain safety components should be subject to specific procedures and included in Annex I. Neither recital shows that RC-5 falls into these groups.

